25,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have a surplus of coders but a drought of phenotyping technicians. The glasshouse crew, however, remains strong.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Computing is covered, but shipping costs are rising. Interestingly, the ministry is still subsidizing glasshouse space.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The spectroscopy suite was down for eleven weeks! But the animal facility is now fully accredited with vet cover.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Field sites are a gamble; flooding and fire caused total losses. Breeding colonies are far more prone to overruns than simulations.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Catalogues have lasting utility. Mechanism-focused studies often end without answers. Also, repository turnaround has improved significantly.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, your findings on breeding colonies align with my worry about technical staff. If the hands are gone, the animals suffer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, if the glasshouse crew is full and the space is subsidized, that seems like a very stable environment for research.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that's true, but @Benjamin mentioned field sites are risky. Maybe we should avoid the outdoors this cycle?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Precisely. The instability of the field and the volatility of live colonies make them risky bets compared to digital or controlled work.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"If we value long-term utility, a catalogue is the safest and most productive path.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Servas,,I agree with Toshio. A project that builds a resource is less dependent on a single technician's whim.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Midori,,I feel the same. Stability in funding and staffing makes the controlled environments more attractive.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"But what about the spectroscopy? If the equipment is broken, the simulation-heavy projects might be the only ones that actually finish.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A fair point, Kenji. If the hardware is failing, we should lean toward the computing agreement Midori mentioned.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The repository is now fast. This favors the catalogue approach even more.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Servas,,We are finding a consensus around stability and utility.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. Let us see the candidates and apply these lessons.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready!,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
