50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have a Microbiome Atlas, Plant Drought Signaling, Protein Folding, and Amphibian Regeneration. The Atlas is a catalogue.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Midori,,"The Plant Drought project uses greenhouses. Since the crew is strong and space is subsidized, it is very viable.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Protein Folding needs spectroscopy, but I saw those logs. It's too risky if the machines are idle.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Amphibians involve breeding colonies and likely field work. Both are high-risk for schedule overruns.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,The Microbiome Atlas is a catalogue. My research shows these provide the most enduring value.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"The Atlas requires sequences and metadata. With the repository turnaround improved, this is highly efficient.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Toshio, do you think the Atlas is more stable than the Plant Drought project?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"The Atlas uses soil samples. If they are already collected, it avoids the field site disasters Benjamin found.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,Exactly. The Atlas is essentially a data project now. It avoids the vivarium costs and the spectroscopy failures.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It is the most rational choice for long-term impact.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,I am inclined toward the Atlas. It is a legacy project.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Midori,,I agree. It balances the current subsidies and the technical strengths we discussed.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'll go with the Atlas too. It's the safest bet for the facilities.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. Logic dictates we avoid the breeding colonies and the broken spectrometers.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,We are in agreement then.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
